Description: OpenPGP certificates that say whose they are
 The PGP ID model gives an OpenPGP certificate a decentralised entity
 identifier: who this key belongs to, said once and checked by people rather
 than by an authority.
 .
 pgpid reads and changes certificates through that model — identifiers,
 validity, ownertrust, addresses, vCard properties, avatars — vouches for
 other people, drives an OpenPGP security key, and puts a secret key on paper
 as QR codes so that any three of five fragments rebuild it.
 .
 Two older shell programs ship alongside: pgpid-gen, which generates a
 certificate from a passport, and pgpid-qrscan, which moves secrets onto a
 smartcard. They need the packages under Suggests.
